7. Trademarks
-------------

**No trademark rights are granted by this Agreement.**

The project's name and mark is "novo-lang".  The word "Novo", where it
appears in this Agreement, in documentation, or in tool output, is an
informal short form of "novo-lang" used descriptively; no rights are
claimed or granted in the word "Novo" standing alone.  The "novo-lang"
name, any project logo, and any other mark used by the project are not
licensed here.  This Agreement grants you rights in the Software's
copyright only.

You may state truthfully that your product is written in novo-lang, is
compatible with novo-lang, or was built with the novo-lang toolchain.
You may not use the project's names or marks as the name of your own
product, as part of your product's name, in a way that suggests the
project endorses, sponsors, or is affiliated with you, or in a way that
is likely to cause confusion about the origin of software.

A distribution of a modified toolchain — which §2 and §3 do not permit in
any case — could not be distributed under the "novo-lang" name.


8. Third-Party Components
-------------------------

The Software incorporates third-party components.  They are identified,
with their licenses, in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, which is part of this
distribution.

**Where a third-party component's license grants you a right this
Agreement would restrict, that license governs that component and this
Agreement does not narrow it.**  Several of the components listed are
copyleft-licensed, and some of their terms — including rights to reverse
engineer for debugging, to obtain source, and to relink — are rights
§3 must not and does not take away.

Nothing in this Agreement is intended to conflict with those licenses.
To the extent of any conflict, the third-party license prevails for the
component it covers.


9. Future Source Release — a Statement of Intent, Not a Promise
---------------------------------------------------------------

The copyright holder intends to publish the full source of the novo-lang
toolchain under the Apache License, Version 2.0, once the compiler is
self-hosting.

**This is a statement of present intent and is NOT a contractual
commitment.**  It creates no obligation, grants no right, and is not
relied upon by this Agreement.  It may change, be delayed, or be
abandoned for any reason or none.  Do not make a decision that depends on
it.

The parts of novo-lang that are already open are already open, today, and are
not waiting on this: the novo-lang C runtime and standard library are licensed
to the public under Apache-2.0 (§4(c), LICENSE-APACHE), and the editor
extension, tree-sitter grammar, playground, and Linguist samples are
licensed under the MIT License in their own directories.


10. Term and Termination
------------------------

This Agreement is effective until terminated.

It terminates automatically, without notice, if you breach any of its
terms.  On termination you must stop using the Software and destroy all
copies of it in your possession.

**Termination does not affect §4.**  Compiler output you produced while
this Agreement was in force remains yours, and the permissions in §4
survive termination permanently.  Losing the right to run the compiler is
not the same as losing the right to ship what you already built with it,
and this Agreement does not conflate them.

Sections 4, 5, 6, 7, and this sentence survive termination.


